---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import DepreciationCalculator from '@/components/tools/calc/DepreciationCalculator.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="depreciation-calculator">
  <DepreciationCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the depreciation calculator works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Straight line: <code>(cost − salvage) ÷ life</code> each year.</li>
      <li>Declining balance: <code>book value × factor ÷ life</code>, with a factor of 2 (double declining) or 1.5. It
        switches to straight line when that gives more, and stops at the salvage value.</li>
      <li>Sum of the years' digits: <code>(cost − salvage) × years left ÷ (life × (life + 1) ÷ 2)</code>.</li>
      <li>MACRS: <code>cost × table percentage</code> for each year, from IRS Publication 946 table A-1 (General
        Depreciation System, half-year convention). Salvage is ignored.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      An asset costs 50,000, has a salvage value of 5,000 and a life of 5 years. Straight line gives 9,000 a year.
      Double declining balance gives 20,000, 12,000, 7,200, 4,320 and 1,480. Sum of the years' digits gives 15,000,
      12,000, 9,000, 6,000 and 3,000. As 5-year MACRS property it gives 10,000, 16,000, 9,600, 5,760, 5,760 and 2,880
      over six tax years.
    </p>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      Years are full years except under MACRS. Mid-quarter and mid-month conventions, bonus depreciation and Section
      179 expensing are not included. Ask a tax adviser which method and class apply to your asset.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
